{
  "documents": [
    {
      "title": "Agreed order scope",
      "text": "Order form — 4 March 2025\nSeller: Kiran, Sora Looms, India\nBuyer: Mela, Tavi Cloth Studio\nPayment: INR 6,400 through PayPal\n\nAgreed requirements:\nDeliver 10 metres of indigo batik print cotton fabric.\nCut the fabric into five separate 2-metre pieces.\nUse colourfast dye that passes a cold-water wash test.\nInclude one printed care card with the fabric.\n\nThe buyer approved this scope before payment. The fabric is intended for a small collection of cushion covers. Packing and courier charges are included in the total above. The seller will send the tracking details after handover; the buyer will confirm the contents after opening the parcel."
    },
    {
      "title": "Delivery and packing note",
      "text": "Packing note — 11 March 2025\nPrepared by Kiran for Mela at Tavi Cloth Studio.\n\nThe parcel contains 10 metres of indigo batik print cotton fabric. Packing count: three separate 2-metre pieces and one continuous 4-metre piece. One printed care card is enclosed in the parcel.\n\nA sample from the same fabric was submitted for a cold-water wash test. The resulting report is in an attachment to the seller's message; its contents are not reproduced in this note.\n\nHanded to India Post on 11 March. Invented tracking reference: EE742681395IN. The parcel was addressed to the buyer's nominated receiving location. The seller sent Mela the tracking details and this packing count on the day of handover."
    },
    {
      "title": "Buyer-seller chat after delivery",
      "text": "15 March 2025\n\n09:12 Mela: The parcel arrived this morning. I measured the indigo fabric: 10 metres in total.\n09:16 Kiran: Thank you for checking. Was the care card inside?\n09:19 Mela: Yes, one printed care card was in the parcel.\n09:23 Mela: I found three 2-metre pieces and one 4-metre piece, not five separate 2-metre pieces.\n09:28 Kiran: That matches my packing note. I should have made the final cut before sending it. I am sorry.\n09:35 Mela: I can arrange the cut here. I have not washed a sample yet, and I cannot open the wash-test report you mentioned.\n09:41 Kiran: I will resend that report separately. Please keep the packaging until we settle the cutting issue."
    }
  ],
